Track 1: The Spindle Bleeds Sweet Water
- Story & Context: On a sweltering July evening inside the mothballed Piedmont Loom Works, night watchman Grady Moss smelled scorched motor oil and clover before discovering an automated shuttle arm rocking a headless steel ribcage beneath the rusted skylight. The robotic chassis tapped a discarded iron bar rhythmically against its own copper frame, generating an otherworldly chime that cut straight through the buzzing Carolina crickets. Mesmerized and terrified, Grady hid behind a stack of unspun bolls of cotton, watching the machine loop its unauthorized sequence until dawn spilled across the floorboards. The Weavers captured that exact incident on magnetic four-track tape with twin weeping slide guitars and mallet runs, honoring Grady’s memory with the fragile opening chorus: "Hush your loose wiring, the morning comes slow."
